    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` are support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `membershipTier` on the owner response with minimal structural impact by keeping the change to small, low-complexity units and never touching the large `Owner` entity class.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/MembershipTier.java`** (new) \u2014 A tiny, cohesive helper mirroring the existing `MembershipNumber`/`CustomerCode` idiom. Its single static `of(namesakeCount, email)` method returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise `\"BRONZE\"`. New class \u21d2 zero surrounding complexity (`WMC_other = 0`).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added one `@Mapping` expression line delegating to `MembershipTier.of(...)`. `OwnerMapper` is a MapStruct interface, so its surrounding complexity is minimal and the mapped method's CC stays 1.\n\nThe `Owner` entity, controllers, and services were left untouched, so the whole class complexity of those larger units never entered the cost. The two acceptance tests (`SILVER` for unique-with-email, `BRONZE` for no-email) and the full suite pass.",
